.TH PBUS-NOTIFY 1 "2026-10-25" "pbus @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pbus-notify \- send a desktop notification from a pbus listener
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pbus-notify
.RI [ options ]
.I summary
.RI [ body ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A desktop notification is a D-Bus message to a daemon running inside a user's
graphical session.
.BR pbusd (8)
runs as root, outside any session, and hands its listeners a scrubbed
environment, so a bare
.BR notify-send (1)
fails with
.IR "Cannot autolaunch D-Bus without X11 $DISPLAY" .
.PP
.B pbus-notify
supplies what is missing: it points D-Bus at the target user's session bus
through
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
and
.BR DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS ,
and, when it runs as root for another user, drops to that user with
.BR setpriv (1)
first. dbus-daemon authenticates its peer by credentials and refuses a uid
that does not own the bus, so dropping privileges is required, not merely
tidy.
.PP
It sends through
.BR notify-send (1)
when that is installed, and through
.BR gdbus (1)
otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u " USER" "\fR, \fP" \-\-user " USER"
Whose desktop to notify. Defaults to
.BR $USER ,
which
.B pbusd
sets to the listener's
.I user
field.
.TP
.BI \-i " NAME" "\fR, \fP" \-\-icon " NAME"
Icon name, by default
.BR dialog-information .
.TP
.BI \-t " MS" "\fR, \fP" \-\-timeout " MS"
How long the popup stays, in milliseconds. Many daemons ignore it.
.TP
.BI \-U " LEVEL" "\fR, \fP" \-\-urgency " LEVEL"
.BR low ", " normal " or " critical .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Sent.
.TP
.B 1
Unknown user.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
That user has no session bus; nobody is logged in to a desktop.
.TP
.B 4
Neither
.B notify-send
nor
.B gdbus
is installed.
.TP
.B 5
Only root can notify another user.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
pbus register-listener release.published --id popup \\
    'pbus-notify -u alice "Release $PBUS_PAYLOAD published"'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Single quotes matter:
.B $PBUS_PAYLOAD
must be expanded when the event fires, not when the listener is registered.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pbus (1),
.BR pbusd (8),
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR setpriv (1)
